+- Award: A prize, honour, decoration, or award category given to a person, group, or work.
+- Broadcast program (a kind of Creative work): A television, radio, or podcast program or series, or one of its seasons.
+- Cause of death: A disease, injury, method, or event named as the cause of a death.
+- Country (a kind of Location): A sovereign, historical, or dependent state or territory.
+- Creative work: A work of authorship or performance not covered by a narrower work type, such as a play or video game.
+- Date: A calendar date, month, or year.
+- Educational institution (a kind of Organization): A school, college, university, or other organization that educates students.
+- Event: Something that happens at a time, such as a battle, competition, ceremony, or campaign.
+- Facility (a kind of Location): A building, structure, or site such as a hospital, cemetery, prison, or airport.
+- Film (a kind of Creative work): A motion picture, a film series, or a dubbed version of a film.
+- Group: Two or more people credited or acting together, such as a band, duo, couple, or team.
+- Human: An individual person, living or historical.
+- Location: A place not covered by a narrower place type, such as a region, river, or island.
+- Musical work (a kind of Creative work): A composition, song, opera, or musical release.
+- Occupation: A profession, job, position, or religious role a person holds.
+- Organization: A formally constituted body such as a company, agency, broadcaster, or society.
+- Product: A manufactured or published product, model, brand, machine, or piece of software.
+- Settlement or region (a kind of Location): A city, town, village, or administrative area below the country level.
+- Written work (a kind of Creative work): A book, periodical, document, or other published text, including legal instruments.
+
+---Relation Types---
+Label each relationship with exactly one of the following relation labels. The `keywords` field of a relationship must be exactly one label from this list, written as listed. Extract only relationships that one of these labels describes. Each line gives the label, the entity types of its source and target, and its definition. For a relation whose target is a date, the target entity is the date as written in the input text.
+
+- award received (Group | Human -> Award | Occupation): award or recognition received by a person, organization or creative work
+- cause of death (Human -> Cause of death): underlying or immediate cause of death
+- child (Group | Human -> Group | Human): subject has object as child
+- composer (Creative work | Musical work -> Group | Human): person(s) who wrote the music
+- country (Location | Organization -> Country | Location | Settlement or region): sovereign state that this subject item is in
+- country of citizenship (Group | Human -> Country | Settlement or region): the object is a country that recognizes the subject as its citizen
+- country of origin (Creative work | Event | Group | Product | Written work -> Country | Location | Organization | Settlement or region): country of origin of this item (creative work, food, phrase, product, etc.)
+- creator (Creative work | Event | Facility | Product | Written work -> Group | Human | Occupation | Organization | Product): maker of this creative work or other object
+- date of birth (Human -> Date): date on which the subject was born
+- date of death (Group | Human -> Date): date on which the subject died
+- director (Broadcast program | Creative work | Film | Musical work | Written work -> Group | Human): director(s) of film, TV-series, stageplay, video game or similar
+- doctoral advisor (Human -> Human): person who supervised the doctorate or PhD thesis of the subject
+- editor (Creative work | Group | Organization | Written work -> Human | Organization): person who checks and corrects a work (such as a book, newspaper, academic journal, etc.) to comply with a rules of certain genre. Also applies to person who establishes the text of an ancient written work or manuscript.
+- educated at (Group | Human -> Educational institution | Event | Facility | Organization): educational institution attended by subject
+- employer (Group | Human -> Broadcast program | Creative work | Educational institution | Event | Facility | Group | Human | Organization | Product | Settlement or region | Written work): person or organization for which the subject works or worked
+- father (Group | Human -> Human): male parent of the subject
+- founded by (Award | Creative work | Event | Facility | Group | Location | Occupation | Organization | Product | Written work -> Group | Human | Organization): founder or co-founder of this organization, religion, place or entity
+- has part (Group -> Human): part of this subject
+- inception (Organization -> Date): time when an entity begins to exist
+- manufacturer (Event | Musical work | Product -> Facility | Human | Occupation | Organization): (main or final) manufacturer or producer of this product
+- mother (Human -> Human): female parent of the subject
+- occupation (Group | Human | Product -> Occupation): occupation of a person
+- performer (Creative work | Event | Human -> Group | Human | Organization): actor, musician, band or other performer associated with this role or musical work
+- place of birth (Group | Human -> Facility | Location): most specific known birth location of a person, animal or fictional character
+- place of burial (Group | Human -> Country | Facility | Location): location of grave, resting place, place of ash-scattering, etc. (e.g., town/city or cemetery) for a person or animal. There may be several places: e.g., re-burials, parts of body buried separately.
+- place of death (Group | Human -> Educational institution | Event | Facility | Location): most specific known (e.g. city instead of country, or hospital instead of city) death location of a person, animal or fictional character
+- place of detention (Event | Group | Human -> Facility | Location | Organization | Settlement or region): place where this person is or was detained
+- presenter (Creative work | Event | Organization -> Human): main role in presenting a radio or television program or a performing arts show
+- producer (Creative work -> Group | Human | Organization): person(s) who produced the film, musical work, theatrical production, etc. (for film, this does not include executive producers, associate producers, etc.)
+- publication date (Creative work | Event | Musical work | Product | Written work -> Date): date or point in time when a work or product was first published or released
+- publisher (Creative work | Musical work | Product | Written work -> Award | Creative work | Educational institution | Organization | Product | Settlement or region | Written work): organization or person responsible for publishing a work, such as a book, periodical, printed music, podcast, game or software
+- sibling (Group | Human -> Group | Human): the subject and the object have at least one common parent (brother, sister, etc. including half-siblings)
+- spouse (Human -> Human): the subject has the object as their spouse (husband, wife, partner, etc.)
+- student of (Group | Human -> Group | Human): person who has taught this person
 
 ---Output Format Template---
